        "object": "<p>The next great climate divide will be between countries that have the resources to adapt and those that don’t</p><p>This summer, much of the media’s attention has focused on record temperatures across Europe and the United States. Television coverage has been filled with familiar images: heat maps shaded deep red, schools closing, rail lines slowing, wildfires spreading and emergency rooms treating growing numbers of people with heat-related illnesses.</p><p>Public officials have responded with equally familiar advice: stay indoors, drink plenty of water and, if possible, turn on the air conditioning.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/jul/15/air-conditioning-access-extreme-heat\">Continue reading...</a>"
